{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 35","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_35\">Problem 35</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 35\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the greatest natural number possessing the property that each of its digits except the first and last one is less than the arithmetic mean of the two neighboring digits. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We seek to maximize the number of digits in the number (call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />) first, so the first and last digits should be 9. Next recognize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> should be symmetric (like 5445 or 93239), and that if there are ever consecutive digits the number cannot contain any digits less than the lower consecutive digit. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> begins with 98, then it must be 9889. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> begins with 97, it can either be 9779, 97679, or 976679. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> begins with 96, it can either be 9669, 96569, 965569, 96469, 964469, 9643469, or 96433469. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> begins with 95, it has the maximum value 95322359, which is less than 96433469. Clearly if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> starts with a lower second digit it is less than this number, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/9/8a9cebd158c2b527ad15811d173d9b049276068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\boxed{96433469}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"127\" height=\"25\" />. Note the differences between consecutive digits in this number.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 34\">Problem 34</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 36\">Problem 36</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_13\" title